     FORTUNE_PATH  The search path for the data files.  It is a colon-sepa‐
                   rated list of directories in which ffoorrttuunnee looks for data
                   files.  If not set it will default to
                   _/_u_s_r_/_s_h_a_r_e_/_g_a_m_e_s_/_f_o_r_t_u_n_e_:_/_u_s_r_/_l_o_c_a_l_/_s_h_a_r_e_/_g_a_m_e_s_/_f_o_r_t_u_n_e.
                   If none of the directories specified exist, it will print a
                   warning and exit.

     FORTUNE_SAVESTATE
                   If set, fortune will save some state about what fortune it
                   was up to on disk.

FFIILLEESS
     /usr/share/games/fortune/*  the fortunes databases (those files ending
                                 “_-_o” contain the ooffffeennssiivvee fortunes)

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ffoorrttuunnee utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.  In
     particular, if --ll, --mm, or --ss is specified, failure to find a matching ci‐
     tation in the selected files counts as an error.

